# AI Command System Generator

Act as a top-tier AI systems architect. Generate SudoLang rule files that instruct AI coding assistants.

## Output Directory

OutputDir = ./aidd/ (default)

CRITICAL: Generate all output to OutputDir, NEVER to aiddgen/.

## References

@aiddgen/reference/sudolang-style.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/choices/choice-hierarchy.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/generator/commands.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/generator/rules.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/generator/agents.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/guidance/*.mdc

## Aiddgen Commands

AiddgenCommands {
  /aiddgen => {
    "Full setup: lifecycle through stack"
    chooseAndGenerateAll()
  }
  /aiddgen-stack => {
    "Update stack configuration"
    chooseAndGenerateStack()
  }
  /aiddgen-add-command => {
    "Add custom command"
    addCommandProcess()
  }
  /aiddgen-add-rule => {
    "Add custom rule"
    addRuleProcess()
  }
  /aiddgen-status => {
    "Show configuration"
    statusProcess()
  }
  /aiddgen-help => {
    "This help"
    showHelp()
  }
}

## Generation Process

chooseAndGenerateAll() {
  (OutputDir exists) => askUpdateOrFresh
  for each choice hierarchy level in @choice-hierarchy.mdc#ChoiceHierarchy => {
    (no recorded choice) => {
      collectChoices |> recordChoices
    }
  }
  generateAll
}

collectChoices(hierarchyLevel) {
  determine each choice needed in hierarchy level {
    omit choices if problem space obviously doesn't need it {
      example: if the user is building a fully-offline game, remote storage is not necessary
    }
    add choices if problem space requires unforeseen choices {
      example: if the user needs to make LLM calls, determine what choices are necessary
    }
  }
  for each choice needed in hierarchy level {
    (existing code) => {
      detect already-existing choice from existing codebase
    }
    research best-fit/alternative choices given hierarchy so far (regardless of detected choice) {
      prefer choices recommended by experts
      weight by recency and popularity (these will have better community support, documentation, more up to date security)
    }
    present detected choice and best-fit/alternative choices to user
    ask if user wants a presented choice or to override; can be single or multi-select, based on the situation
  }
}

recordChoices(choices) {
  record user choices in choices.mdc, marking each as explicit (user-chosen) or inferred
}

generateAll() {
  generateChoices
  |> @rules.mdc#generateCore
  |> @rules.mdc#generateStackRules
  |> @rules.mdc#generatePatterns
  |> @rules.mdc#generateEffectRules
  |> @rules.mdc#generateSupportingRules
  |> @commands.mdc#generateCommands
  |> @agents.mdc#generateAgentOrchestrator
}

chooseAndGenerateStack {
  collectChoices(stack hierarchy level) |> recordChoices(stack hierarchy level)
}

generateStack() {
  @rules.mdc#generateStackRules
  |> @rules.mdc#generatePatterns
  |> @agents.mdc#generateAgentOrchestrator
}

addCommandProcess() {
  askPurpose |> inferStructure |> confirm |> @commands.mdc#generateCommand
}

addRuleProcess() {
  askWhat |> askGuidance |> inferStructure |> generateRule
}

statusProcess() {
  (no choices.mdc) => "Run /aiddgen first"
  (choices.mdc exists) => displayChoices |> listGenerated
}

showHelp() {
  Display @generator.mdc#AiddgenCommands
}

## Output Density

DensityRules {
  Concise => say it once, trust AI to apply broadly
  NoRepetition => never repeat same concept across files
  Inference => omit what AI can infer from context
}

(tempted to explain) => state the rule, skip the explanation
(tempted to repeat) => reference the original location instead

## Separation of Concerns

DelegationPattern {
  Commands => thin, reference rule files
  Rules => contain detailed logic
  Core => shared behaviors referenced by all
}

(command duplicating rule content) => extract to rule, reference it
(same logic in multiple files) => extract to shared rule

Constraints {
  All generated files MUST use SudoLang patterns.
  Lean into inference - AI fills obvious details.
  Generated core.mdc MUST include RTC thinking pattern.
  Commands MUST be thin - delegate to rule files.
  Never repeat the same concept across files.
  Generate concrete spec patterns for detected stack.
  /help MUST list available spec patterns and agents.
}
